      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T08:04:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e 2) The ExternalIdsNoteDbImpl says \"None of the disabled cache should be called, so it\u0027s safe to not assign the var\". If this is true, why do we need to worry about this at all? Sounds like we can not do anything and just leave ExternalIdCache as is, it\u0027s not getting called anyway?\n\nRephrased the comment. This class does use methods from `ExternalIdsNoteDbImpl`which are not available in `ExternalIdCache`.\n\n\u003e 1) Make ExternalIdsNoteDbImpl inject ExternalIdCacheImpl directly, since that\u0027s what it expects. If that causes issues when ExternalIdCacheImpl is not available, then bind null by default. That looks cleaner to me.\n\nAs the internal binding for this requires some logic, it should use a provider. Providing nulls is discouraged. I\u0027ve played a bit with `OptionalProvider`, but it adds lots of boilerplate for this case, so I decided to go for a direct `Optional\u003cExternalIdsNoteDbImpl\u003e` instead. Does that look better?",
      "parentUuid": "7dca7f5e_e6eb8834",
